  "term": "acetaldehyde",
  "definition": "Acetaldehyde is a colorless, flammable liquid used in making acetic acid, perfumes, and flavorings. In mental health contexts, it is relevant as a substance formed during alcohol metabolism that has general narcotic effects and can irritate mucous membranes; very large amounts can stop breathing and cause death.",
